<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Timeline — Renato Molina Toth</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Career timeline and projects." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="noise"></div>
    <div class="bg-glow bg-glow-1"></div>
    <div class="bg-glow bg-glow-2"></div>

    <div class="container">
      <nav>
        <a href="/">Me</a>
        <a href="/timeline" class="nav-active">Journey</a>
      </nav>

      <header>
        <h1>Timeline</h1>
      </header>

      <section class="timeline">
        <div class="tl-track">
          <div class="tl-track-progress" id="track-progress"></div>
        </div>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.02">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2025 - Present</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Chief Technology Officer</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Skillsetter · Vancouver, BC</p>
            <p>Setting technical vision and scaling the engineering team. Owning SOC 2 compliance and GDPR adherence. Driving AI strategy and product direction across the platform.</p>
            <a href="https://skillsetter.com" target="_blank" class="tl-link">skillsetter.com →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.04">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2024 - 2025</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Principal Software Engineer & Team Lead</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Skillsetter · Vancouver, BC</p>
            <p>Led the technical strategy and development of the core application. Architected web applications and RESTful APIs in Ruby on Rails. Engineered AI capabilities integrating OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Gemini, and ElevenLabs. Implemented real-time video with WebRTC and LMS integrations (Blackboard, Canvas). Managed cloud infrastructure on AWS (EC2, RDS, SNS, Docker).</p>
            <a href="https://skillsetter.com" target="_blank" class="tl-link">skillsetter.com →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.03">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2016 - 2024</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Senior Software Engineer</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Skillsetter · Vancouver, BC</p>
            <p>Built the platform from the ground up. Full-stack development in Ruby on Rails, scaling architecture on AWS, and establishing engineering practices that grew with the company.</p>
            <a href="https://skillsetter.com" target="_blank" class="tl-link">skillsetter.com →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.04">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2016 - 2018</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Senior Software Engineer</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Noomii · Vancouver, BC</p>
            <p>Developed and maintained a cloud-based coaching marketplace in Ruby on Rails. Designed scalable architecture on AWS, integrated third-party services (Intercom, Stripe), and migrated the platform from Ruby 1.9 to 2.4. Applied reverse engineering techniques to document legacy systems.</p>
            <a href="https://www.noomii.com" target="_blank" class="tl-link">noomii.com →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.03">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2014 - 2015</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Tech Lead Software Engineer</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Inspira Tecnologia · São Paulo, Brazil</p>
            <p>Led Android and Ruby teams across multiple web and mobile projects. Served as Scrum Master, designed APIs and mobile apps (Android SDK, PhoneGap), and consulted for startups on technical and business strategy. Acted as an innovation agent applying UX techniques.</p>
            <a href="https://www.inspira.com.br/" target="_blank" class="tl-link">inspira.com.br →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.05">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2013 - 2014</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Chief Technology Officer</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Jazz · São Paulo, Brazil</p>
            <p>Managed and led projects with a multidisciplinary team. Designed an innovation process for different business contexts, from understanding user needs through UX research to choosing architecture, process, and technology. Mentored developers in the Android Jam Program and designed the company's career plan for technology, design, and management.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.02">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2013</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Chief Technology Officer & Co-founder</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Doog™ · Brazil</p>
            <p>Co-founded a B2B startup focused on geolocation and tracking salesforce and products. Led technology decisions, product design, and the development team. Built mobile apps (Android SDK, PhoneGap) and backend APIs in Ruby on Rails. Managed investor relations and served as board member. Applied lean and agile principles to the company's internal processes.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.04">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2012 - 2013</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Software Engineer Consultant</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Brasil RFID / Inovacode Solutions · São Paulo, Brazil</p>
            <p>Developed an RFID system with Android app and Ruby on Rails backend. Conducted technological feasibility studies, migrated a legacy system to a new architecture, and designed the integration API.</p>
            <a href="https://www.inovacode.com.br/" target="_blank" class="tl-link">inovacode.com.br →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.03">
          <div class="tl-beacon beacon-gold"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg></div>
          <time>2012</time>
          <div class="tl-card card-award">
            <span class="tl-badge award">Award</span>
            <h2>Interaction South America</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">IxDA / Agência Click</p>
            <p>2nd place in Best Mobile Applications, Innovation and Usability category. Recognized across Latin America.</p>
            <a href="https://ixda.org/initiatives/interaction-latin-america/" target="_blank" class="tl-link">ixda.org →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.02">
          <div class="tl-beacon beacon-green"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09z"/><path d="M12 15l-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.35 22.35 0 0 1-4 2z"/><path d="M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0"/><path d="M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5"/></svg></div>
          <time>2011</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge project">Project</span>
            <h2>Inverse Maxi</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">CESAR · Shipped product</p>
            <p>One of the first smart fridges in the Brazilian market. Developed the Android OS customization and the integration layer between the embedded system and the refrigerator API, enabling a tablet component to control the fridge. Full lifecycle from prototype to mass production.</p>
            <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G34Dra2v85c" target="_blank" class="tl-link">Watch demo →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.03">
          <div class="tl-beacon beacon-green"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09z"/><path d="M12 15l-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.35 22.35 0 0 1-4 2z"/><path d="M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0"/><path d="M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5"/></svg></div>
          <time>2011</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge project">Project</span>
            <h2>Positivo Ypy</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">CESAR · Shipped product</p>
            <p>Android OS customization and applications for one of Brazil's first consumer tablets. Deep system-level work on the platform. Reached hundreds of thousands of users.</p>
            <a href="https://www.positivotecnologia.com.br" target="_blank" class="tl-link">positivotecnologia.com.br →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.04">
          <div class="tl-beacon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg></div>
          <time>2011 - 2013</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge role">Role</span>
            <h2>Systems Engineer</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">CESAR · Sorocaba, Brazil</p>
            <p>Developed systems focused on innovation in mobile, embedded systems, web, and interactive TV. Built product backlogs with product owners, applied UX research (focus groups, interviews, prototyping), and led Android OS customizations for specific product contexts.</p>
            <a href="https://www.cesar.org.br" target="_blank" class="tl-link">cesar.org.br →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.03">
          <div class="tl-beacon beacon-purple"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M22 10v6M2 10l10-5 10 5-10 5z"/><path d="M6 12v5c0 2 2 3 6 3s6-1 6-3v-5"/></svg></div>
          <time>2011 - 2012</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge education">Education</span>
            <h2>M.Sc. Computer Science (incomplete)</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Universidade Federal de São Carlos (UFSCar)</p>
            <p>Compilers and programming languages research. Investigated macro systems in Cyan for domain-specific language generation.</p>
            <a href="https://cyan-lang.org/" target="_blank" class="tl-link">cyan-lang.org →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.05">
          <div class="tl-beacon beacon-purple"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M22 10v6M2 10l10-5 10 5-10 5z"/><path d="M6 12v5c0 2 2 3 6 3s6-1 6-3v-5"/></svg></div>
          <time>2008 - 2011</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge education">Education</span>
            <h2>B.Sc. Computer Science</h2>
            <p class="tl-org">Universidade Federal de São Carlos (UFSCar)</p>
            <p>Research on compilers and OLAP systems. Co-founded and organized SeCoT, a tech conference that brought global speakers to campus across three editions.</p>
            <a href="https://www.ufscar.br" target="_blank" class="tl-link">ufscar.br →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tl-entry" data-speed="1.02">
          <div class="tl-beacon beacon-purple"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M22 10v6M2 10l10-5 10 5-10 5z"/><path d="M6 12v5c0 2 2 3 6 3s6-1 6-3v-5"/></svg></div>
          <time>2006</time>
          <div class="tl-card">
            <span class="tl-badge education">Education</span>
            <h2>Tech Instructor</h2>
